From 892eb1557b14c3cb17ca910d6f13bbff31929710 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nex <63727521+LuCiLuna@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:09:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 026/114] ASoC: codecs: add NXP TFA9874 amplifier driver

The TFA9874 has no on-chip DSP (speaker protection runs on the host DSP),
so it only needs its registers programmed: the NXP "optimal settings" for
the silicon revision, the board's container settings, TDM slot layout for
the stream, then power up once the PLL has locked to BCK.

Settings are taken from the NXP tfa98xx driver and the OnePlus 9 Pro
tfa98xx.cnt "speaker" profile. No speaker protection or volume control yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
